<article class="env-lemma" id="010Y">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/010Y">Lemma <span data-tag="010Y">12.13.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The category of chain complexes in $\mathcal{A}$ is abelian. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A morphism of complexes $f : A_\bullet \to B_\bullet $ is injective if and only if each $f_ n : A_ n \to B_ n$ is injective. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A morphism of complexes $f : A_\bullet \to B_\bullet $ is surjective if and only if each $f_ n : A_ n \to B_ n$ is surjective. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A sequence of chain complexes 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  A_\bullet \xrightarrow {f} B_\bullet \xrightarrow {g} C_\bullet  \]
</div>
<p>
 is exact at $B_\bullet $ if and only if each sequence 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  A_ i \xrightarrow {f_ i} B_ i \xrightarrow {g_ i} C_ i  \]
</div>
<p>
 is exact at $B_ i$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>